    "review_summary": [
      "Independently reviewed all 86 frozen scope artifacts; every path was present and every SHA-256 exactly matched the fixed scope. The eight generated own formal pages were read, and the actual-preview-005 receipt reports passed=true and actual_own_formal_pages_checked=8.",
      "Inventory/UI association is exact: 2 implementations and 4 bindings—Combat Sword P2 Marks I/II/III (Heavy Sword Turtolsky Mk VI/VII/IX) and Paired Transonic Blades P1 Mark I (Branx Mk XI). The similar Power Sword P1 metadata-only definition has no matching inventory binding and is correctly excluded.",
      "Both complete I–IV tier series and wrappers agree with the formal pages: Combat Sword P2 contributes .05/.06/.07/.08 melee rending per effective layer; Paired Transonic P1 contributes .04/.05/.06/.07; both use 2.5/3/3.5/4 seconds. Own parent-context overrides replace the child fallback, rather than add to it.",
      "The paired RAW name and description use the same language-resource hash; formatter reconstruction for all grades and both implementations preserves the displayed percent prefix, duration, and four-stack text. The localization comparison correctly classifies target-count, item/held, latch, refresh, expiry, and damage-calculation details as omitted by the RAW rather than mistranslations.",
      "The event route is consistent across the four bound Marks: the second or later qualifying melee target event in the same Sweep can request one layer only when the source item matches and the weapon is still held. Ordinary, heavy, actual special-sweep, and push-follow Sweep hits can meet those gates; standalone pure push is attack_type=push and does not qualify, special-mode toggles are not hit events, and the scanned action tables contain no projectile/ranged route. No kill or positive-damage gate is claimed.",
      "The layer lifecycle is internally consistent: at most one child request per Sweep; up to four effective layers; a successful qualifying proc refreshes the shared timer even at cap; expiry removes the active layer set together. Event damage precedes queued proc/cache work, so the triggering hit is not retroactively changed and the pages do not promise same-frame effect on a later target. Held state controls proc/stat contribution after cache update; an existing timer continues while switched away, a still-live effect can return on switching back, and destroying/removing the parent clears its controlled child.",
      "The controlled Transonic Branx Mk XI light_linesman example correctly selects target_index=1 armored lerp_0_75 (.48/1.02), excludes crit_mod under the stated noncritical premise, and uses t=.5 to derive A=.75. With Tier I R=.04, neutral other modifiers, armored factor 1, and illustrative B=100, the armor stage is 75→79, a 4/75≈5.33% relative increase at that stage; it is not presented as universal final HP damage.",
      "The icon evidence maps the actual trait icon 179 to the reviewed public image receipt (128×128, HTTP 200, PNG SHA-256 2c41c33cfe663e24503c651428e847a39e352b628cdfe71cb13b254352aa5e3a), and the map, reverse/catalog entries, per-weapon pages, and association snapshot agree on the two variants/four bindings.",
      "The localization-comparison rules table uses concise source basenames and line ranges; I cross-checked these against the adjacent SOURCE_INDEX full-path pinned links and the fixed source/evidence hashes. This is traceable and did not create a content or citation blocker."
    ],
